      "content": "Dosing adjustments should only ever be made under direct medical supervision. Taking a half dose of Adderall could potentially help with your focus temporarily, but distributing your doses in this way can interfere with their effectiveness and lead to unpredictable results. It's crucial to keep taking your medication exactly as prescribed until you speak with your doctor. Instead, try to find a temporary coping strategy for your jitters, such as deep breathing exercises, moderate exercise, or moving to a quieter space if possible. Until your appointment, your doctor might allow a phone consultation or recommend over-the-counter remedies that can help manage mild symptoms, but it's best to have their guidance.",
